  "body": "Adds a local-only browser fingerprint laboratory for defensive research without changing FlipBot's production marketplace runtime.\n\nHighlights:\n- standalone `pl.flipbot.playwright.lab.fingerprint` package; no imports into BrowserManager/BotContext/login/scanner/negotiation code\n- explicit `FLIPBOT_FINGERPRINT_LAB=true` gate\n- hard target allowlist: loopback, `*.localhost`, and reserved `*.test` hosts only\n- HTTP(S) routing aborts external requests\n- Service Workers blocked so they cannot bypass request interception\n- WebSockets routed separately; only allowed lab hosts can connect\n- self-contained loopback detector server on `127.0.0.1:18091`\n- baseline-vs-synthetic Chrome comparison\n- synthetic lab profile covering navigator, screen/DPR, locale/timezone, WebGL and canvas surfaces\n- deliberate tamper marker and no native-function-source forgery, so defensive checks can detect hooks\n- detector page checks UA Client Hints, window-vs-worker consistency, API integrity, webdriver, media/capability signals, WebGL and canvas\n- policy and safety regression tests\n- PowerShell usage guide in `playwright/FINGERPRINT_LAB.md`\n\nThe lab intentionally does not provide production-site stealth or CAPTCHA/anti-bot bypass behavior.",
